  "summary": "Connect native hub splitting, scatter and cooperative averaging to imported frames and correct body-index coloring groups.",
  "regressions": [
    "One and two dynamic plates each with 33 ball contacts, at frames one and eight, must match a fresh production RbdPipeline trace.",
    "Independent exact reservation totals, membership, ownership, mass scaling, tile slots and guards; valid atomic reservation permutation accepted and matching corrupt actual/reference outputs rejected.",
    "Body/collider index spaces remain separate: BodyGroup is identity over bodies, regardless of multi-collider parent arrays.",
    "Adjacency scans cover all body slots; solver velocity allocation includes the native hub pool and outer guards.",
    "513 actual independent batches exercise a 1026-slot native pool; fixture padding must not increase native hub capacity.",
    "Rust public runtime integration starts with pair capacity one and checks hub trajectories through automatic growth and untraced continuation."
  ],
  "differences": [
    "Uses separate ordered color dispatches with hub scatter/average around every contact pass. Ascend hardware barriers remain unvalidated.",
    "Hub slot/list atomic allocation order is not cross-device identity. Only verified slot fields are resolved to semantic body/contact identities; physical outputs retain default tolerances.",
    "Existing non-import fixture scenes retain their hub-disabled schedule. No Rust production shader arithmetic was changed."
  ]
